      <h2>What makes a London &amp; South East move different</h2>
      <p>Relocating within or out of London and the South East brings a specific set of pressures that a straightforward regional move doesn&rsquo;t. Property chains here often run longer than the UK average, so timing a sale against a purchase elsewhere takes careful management &mdash; the kind of coordination our chauffeur-driven viewings and estate agent liaison exist for.</p>
      <p>Many of the homes we help clients leave are leasehold flats, which means factoring in service charges, managing agents and remaining lease length alongside the usual sale process &mdash; details we build into your move plan from the first consultation. And because property values in this region are typically higher, the decision to downsize, release equity, or move closer to family often carries more financial complexity than a like-for-like move elsewhere in the country.</p>
      <p>Practical logistics matter more here too: parking suspensions, loading restrictions and, in central London, the Congestion and Ultra Low Emission Zones all need factoring into moving-day planning, along with building-specific rules many flats and managed developments have around lift booking and permitted access hours for removal vehicles. We plan around these before moving day, not on it.</p>
      <div class="area-honest">
        <p>We&rsquo;re based in Northampton and work with clients across the UK, including throughout London and the South East. Your dedicated coordinator manages the process remotely and in person as needed &mdash; chauffeur-driven viewings, on-the-ground staging visits and moving day itself are all covered, wherever in the region you&rsquo;re moving from or to.</p>
      </div></div>
